    <string name="settings_autostart_desc">Samsung calls this \"Sleeping apps\", others call it \"Autostart\" or \"Protected Apps\" (Xiaomi, Oppo, Vivo, Infinix, etc.) — needed for background playback to survive</string>
    <string name="settings_allow_background">Open App Battery Settings</string>
    <string name="settings_allow_background_desc">On Infinix specifically, look for \"Battery Saver\" or \"Battery\" here and enable \"Allow Background Running\"</string>
    <string name="allow_background_dialog_message">On the next screen, tap \"Battery\" or \"Battery Saver\", then turn on \"Allow Background Running\" (Berjalan di Latar Belakang). Also check \"Permissions\" for a toggle called \"Pause app activity if unused\" and turn that OFF.</string>
    <string name="autostart_not_found_message">Couldn\'t open it automatically for this phone. Samsung: Settings \u2192 Battery and device care \u2192 Battery \u2192 Background usage limits \u2192 add Music Player to \"Never sleeping apps\". Oppo: Phone Manager \u2192 App management \u2192 Startup Manager, then also set \"Allow background running\" for this app. Vivo: Settings \u2192 More settings \u2192 Applications \u2192 Autostart. Others: look for \"Autostart\", \"Protected Apps\", or \"Phone Manager\" / \"Security\" app.</string>
